## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical use of MVCC, isolation levels, and atomic write patterns in a real transactional system.

## Key Concepts

- SERIALIZABLE vs REPEATABLE READ
- SELECT ... FOR UPDATE
- Write skew, serialization failures, retry backoff

## Code Example

```sql
BEGIN;
SET TRANSACTION ISOLATION LEVEL SERIALIZABLE;
SELECT balance FROM accounts WHERE id = $1 FOR UPDATE;
UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance - $3 WHERE id = $1 AND balance >= $3;
UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance + $3 WHERE id = $2;
INSERT INTO transfers(from_id,to_id,amount,created_at,status) VALUES($1,$2,$3,now(),'completed');
COMMIT;
```

